  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You had an array AAA of size NNN, and a cost array CCC of size NNN.\n\nYou will do exactly NNN operations of the following type:\n\n\nChoose iii such that 1≤i≤∣A∣1 \\le i \\le |A|1≤i≤∣A∣, and then delete AiA_iAi​ from the array AAA.\nThe associated cost of this operation is Ai×CiA_i \\times C_iAi​×Ci​.\nAfter each operation, the remaining parts of AAA are concatenated and re-indexed from 111 to ∣A∣|A|∣A∣.\nNote that the array CCC is not modified.\n\nFind the minimum total cost needed to perform the NNN operations, thus deleting AAA.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN - the size of the arrays.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - A1,A2,A3,…,ANA_1, A_2, A_3, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,A3​,…,AN​.\nThe third line contains NNN integers - C1,C2,C3,…,CNC_1, C_2, C_3, \\ldots, C_NC1​,C2​,C3​,…,CN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the minimum cost to delete the array AAA.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1001 \\le T \\le 1001≤T≤100",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤Ai,Ci≤1001 \\le A_i, C_i \\le 1001≤Ai​,Ci​≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n4 2\n2 1\n2\n4 2\n1 2\n5\n1 1 1 1 1\n10 4 7 5 3",
        "output": "10\n6\n25",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : We first choose index i=2i = 2i=2, for a cost of 2⋅1=22 \\cdot 1 = 22⋅1=2. Updated array A=[4]A = [4]A=[4]. Then, choose i=1i = 1i=1 for a cost of 4⋅24 \\cdot 24⋅2. Total cost is 101010.\nTest Case 2 : Choose i=1i = 1i=1 twice. The costs are 444 and 222 for the operations, thus a sum of 666."
      }
    ]
